@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Privacy audit
+
+Scope: account forms, shared page layout, document headers, and the linked privacy notice.
+
+| Finding | Change |
+| --- | --- |
+| Analytics ran on every page, including account pages. | Removed the analytics script and dormant advertising script reference. No consent-dependent tracker is loaded by the layout. |
+| Font requests contacted Google on ordinary visits. | Removed remote font stylesheets and preconnects; use device serif fonts. |
+| Forms did not identify the recipient or purpose of credentials. | Added notices before submission, pseudonymous username guidance, and a privacy link. Kept only username and password; no extra consent or profile fields. |
+| Backend error text could expose account details. | Show generic errors without rendering the service response. |
+| Credential requests could disclose the page URL or follow redirects. | Explicitly omit cookies and referrers, disable caching, reject redirects, and clear passwords after each attempt. No tokens or credentials are saved in browser storage. |
+| Forms had no explicit POST fallback or password-manager hints. | Use POST semantics and autocomplete hints; disable inputs until hydration so credentials cannot accidentally enter a URL before JavaScript loads. Enforce the displayed registration password requirements. |
+| Page visits initialized empty reading-list sessions. | Remove automatic initialization; the existing bookmark POST creates the list when requested. |
+| Documents lacked privacy headers. | Add no-referrer policy (HTTP and HTML), disable camera/microphone/geolocation/topics, prevent MIME sniffing, restrict form targets/embeds/framing, and prevent response caching. |
+| Privacy text was generic and the preferences link was inert. | Describe actual data flows and limitations; link the footer to actionable browser and reading-list choices. |
+
+## Boundaries and remaining work
+
+The external account service is outside this repository. Its password handling, retention, operational logs, rate limiting, account deletion/export, and any session mechanism need a separate backend review. The frontend previously discarded returned authentication tokens and still does; this work does not implement a persistent login session. No account deletion or retention guarantees are invented in the notice.
+
+External article images and article-specific demonstration scripts remain. Removing shared analytics does not establish that every content page makes no external requests. The privacy notice describes external image connections; document-level no-referrer protection applies to them too.
+
+Validation uses the production build and automated source/isolated component checks only. No browser verification, server startup, server entrypoint import, or live credential submissions are needed.
