-    <h2>1. An overview of data protection</h2>
-    <p><strong>General information</strong></p>
-    <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. The term “personal data” comprises all data that can be used to personally identify you. For detailed information about the subject matter of data protection, please consult our Data Protection Declaration, which we have included beneath this copy.</p>
-    
-    <h2>2. General information and mandatory information</h2>
-    <p><strong>Data protection</strong></p>
-    <p>The operators of this website and its pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously. Hence, we handle your personal data as confidential information and in compliance with the statutory data protection regulations and this Data Protection Declaration.</p>
-    <p>Whenever you use this website, a variety of personal information will be collected. Personal data comprises data that can be used to personally identify you. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect as well as the purposes we use this data for. It also explains how, and for which purpose the information is collected.</p>
-    
-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <h2>Account information</h2>
+    <p>Browsing articles does not require an account. The sign-up and sign-in forms ask only for a username and password. You can choose a username that does not identify you; we do not ask for your real name, email address, or demographic information.</p>
+    <p>Only submitting a form sends these credentials over HTTPS to the account service at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net</code>, using its <code>/times_cdn/api/register</code> or <code>/times_cdn/api/login</code> endpoint. The service is hosted on Google Cloud and receives connection information such as your IP address. These requests omit browser cookies and the referring page URL.</p>
+    <p>The forms use this information to request account creation or sign-in. They clear the password field after each request and do not save passwords or returned tokens in browser storage. Your browser's password manager may offer to remember credentials according to your settings.</p>
+
+    <h2>Reading lists and storage</h2>
+    <p>Saving an article stores its identifier in a server-side reading-list session. A session cookie lets the site retrieve that list on later requests. Ordinary page visits do not initialize an empty reading list. You can remove saved articles with the bookmark control and clear this site's cookies in your browser to disconnect your browser from the session.</p>
+
+    <h2>Scripts, fonts, and external content</h2>
+    <p>The shared page layout does not load third-party analytics or advertising scripts. Fonts use those already available on your device, without contacting a font provider. Some articles contain externally hosted images; loading these images contacts the image host, which receives connection information such as your IP address. Pages use a no-referrer policy to avoid sending the referring page URL.</p>
+    <p>The site host and account service may maintain operational logs. This website's source does not establish those services' log retention, account retention, or password storage practices; this notice does not promise a particular deletion period or storage method for those services.</p>
+
+    <h2 id="privacy-choices">Your privacy choices</h2>
+    <p>You can read without registering, choose a pseudonymous username, remove reading-list entries, and manage site cookies and saved passwords through your browser. The shared layout does not enable optional analytics or advertising scripts. These forms do not request marketing preferences.</p>
+    <p>For operator information, see the <a href={`${baseUrl}legal/imprint`}>imprint</a>. Self-service account export and deletion controls are not currently available on this site.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
